    narr:childCount "29"^^xsd:integer ;
    narr:generatedFrom "7197e2e5261482e8ab862a8aa0f16ad8ffe0fb2f" ;
    narr:narration """An advisory call, narrated in speaking order. The requester opens by [framing the ask as an outside read before the board, not a programme invitation](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_1), and the advisor accepts with a [pledge to be blunt where useful and quiet where not](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_2). The plan under review is [a four-site sequential migration off a vendor platform, with soak periods, replica reporting, and vendor-held reference data](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_3). The advisor's endorsement rests on [precedent: two big-bang programmes went backwards, the sequential one was boring and finished](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_5), and he [urges holding the sequence against pressure dressed as efficiency](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_7), advising [writing down the rationale now, in calm, before month-four pressure arrives](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_9). The critique follows a forewarning: [the plan has no data-quality gate — nothing stops a site cutting over with bad data](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_13); a validation step [tells you data moved, not that it was any good](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_15). He defines the gate as [a named quality bar measured on source, with a remediation queue and an owner who isn't the programme manager](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_17), [insisting the structure, not a personal judgment, keeps the tempted person from holding the gate](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_19), and [budgeting for at least one gate-fired delay](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_21) — [if it never stops anything, it isn't a gate](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_23). He also [endorses the reference-data call with a caveat on the mirror's refresh interval, and directs the archive work be done](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_25). The requester [concedes the gate critique is fair and new](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_20), [commits to presenting it to the board as a named open item](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_28), and the advisor closes [endorsing that: bring them a hole you've named](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_29).""" ;
